# ── Aspire ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generated and local-only. `.aspire/modules/` is regenerated by `aspire restore`
# — treat it like node_modules. Deliberately NOT a blanket `.aspire/` ignore:
# that folder can also hold project config worth committing, and silently
# swallowing it is exactly the kind of thing this file is meant to prevent.
# If Aspire starts writing something new there, decide about it explicitly.
**/.aspire/modules/
**/.aspire/backchannels/
**/.aspire/cache/
aspire-output/
.aspire-manifest.json


# ── Angular / Node ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
# Angular's build output is redirected here so AegisScribe.Web can serve it
# directly (.claude/rules/gateway.md → "The web host") — generated, not source.
src/AegisScribe.Web/wwwroot/
tmp/
out-tsc/
bazel-out/
.angular/
*.tsbuildinfo
.npm/
.yarn/
.pnpm-store/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache


# ── .NET MAUI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Platform build output is covered by bin/obj above; these are the extras.
# Signing material is in the credentials section — an Android keystore or an
# Apple provisioning profile in the repo is the mobile equivalent of committing
# a private key, because it lets someone else ship a build as you.
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa
*.app.zip
*.dSYM/
*.xcarchive/
[Pp]latforms/[Aa]ndroid/**/[Rr]esource.designer.cs
Resource.Designer.cs

# Firebase / APNs client config. Not secret — it ships inside the app, and
# .claude/rules/mobile.md is clear that anything on a device is public — but it
# is environment-specific, so the repo shouldn't carry one team's project.
# Commit a *.example alongside if the setup steps need one.
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
!google-services.example.json
!GoogleService-Info.example.plist


# ── SQL Server and other local data ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Aspire runs SQL Server in a container with a Docker-managed data volume, so
# these mostly appear when someone attaches a local database by hand.
*.mdf
*.ldf
*.ndf
*.bak
*.bacpac
*.dtsx.user
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-shm
*.db-wal


# ── Playwright / e2e ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.playwright-mcp/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
playwright/.auth/
test-results/
.last-run.json


# ── Claude Code ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The rest of `.claude/` is committed on purpose — the toolkit is as much the
# point of this repo as the app. Only personal overrides and anything
# credential-shaped comes out.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.credentials.json
.claude/**/*.local.*
CLAUDE.local.md


