*.rej


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  DO NOT IGNORE THESE — they look like build output or config, and are source
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  .claude/                        The toolkit. Rules, skills, agents, hooks.
#  .claude/settings.json           Shared hook wiring — the local override is
#                                  settings.local.json, which IS ignored above.
#  .mcp.json                       MCP server config, incl. the pinned port 8765
#                                  that pairs with the AppHost endpoint.
#  CLAUDE.md                       Project memory, loaded every session.
#  **/Migrations/*.cs              EF Core migrations are SOURCE, not output.
#                                  The vector index needs reviewed raw SQL.
#  contract/openapi.v1.json        The API contract. It is committed BECAUSE it
#                                  is generated — the diff is how a breaking
#                                  change gets noticed before a shipped mobile
#                                  client does. See .claude/rules/api-contract.md.
#  design/aegisscribe-armory.html  The visual source of truth. No build step.
#  Directory.Build.props
#  Directory.Packages.props        Central package management.
#  global.json                     Pins the SDK.
#  .editorconfig
#  .gitattributes                  Keeps the shell hooks LF — see that file.
#  **/launchSettings.json          Committed on purpose so ports and profiles are
#                                  shared. It must therefore hold NO secrets:
#                                  credentials are Aspire parameters read from
#                                  user secrets (.claude/rules/aspire.md).
